WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.250
- [Kelly] Was it weird when
they asked you to play yourself?

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.140
Because it's an exaggerated version

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.250
of yourself.
- Very strange.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.330
- Yeah.
- It was the most

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.980
daunting thing I've ever done.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.120
Because I --
- When you first read it,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.620
were you into it?
- No.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.560
I was like, no muscle in my body tells me

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.520
to make this movie.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.230
I like to hide behind a character.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.060
But this character's name is Nick Cage.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.200
I mean, what are you guys gonna do

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.100
to me?
- Dude!

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.780
- There's other Cages running around.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:22.890
I don't wanna humiliate them.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:25.080
I don't wanna humiliate myself.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:25.980
- Yeah.
- And I was worried.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.870
- You didn't it. It's brilliant!

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:28.703
- [Nicolas] Well, thank you.

00:00:28.703 --> 00:00:30.420
But I thought it might lapse until like

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.390
in Andy Sandberg Saturday
Night Live sketch

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.380
or something.
- No.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.760
- Thankfully, I had a good director

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.350
and he kept it about people.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.120
So that was --
- A great director.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.147
- [Nicolas] Thank you.
- And it's like.

00:00:40.147 --> 00:00:40.980
(audience clapping)

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.110
It's amazing how the story unfolds.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.720
And like, you don't see some stuff coming.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.788
The LSD trip in the car.
- Oh my gosh!

00:00:47.788 --> 00:00:48.760
(both laughing)

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.254
- It's like, amazing. (laughs)

00:00:51.254 --> 00:00:52.470
- It's funny.
- Like how you look at him

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.360
and how Pascal looks like.
- Yeah.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.440
He's so good.
- Pedro Pascal.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.640
Yeah. It was amazing.
- Yeah.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.473
- You two.

00:00:57.473 --> 00:00:59.010
Your chemistry,

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.630
it's amazing!
- Thank you.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.270
- Like I love when you get like,

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.040
starts together that you didn't,

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.060
I don't know, I didn't picture it.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.060
And then you're, and it's like
the most amazing chemistry.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:09.893
- [Nicolas] Well, thank you.

00:01:09.893 --> 00:01:12.510
Now. He is not only a great actor,

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.130
he's such a nice man.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.320
And it's easy to work with Pedro.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.200
You know, it was kind of like
we had similar interests.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.360
We love movies and we would
just talk about movies.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.980
Kind of like the way
you and I are talking,

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:23.970
and then the director says, "Action".

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.680
- That's kinda like
what your characters do.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.520
- [Nicolas] Yeah.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.630
Just talking about movies.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.160
And then we would say action,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.500
and we just kept the conversation going.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.007
- [Kelly] Wait, speaking of action.

00:01:33.007 --> 00:01:36.090
That's my favorite part. (laughs)

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:38.520
There's a part in the film
where he's out. (laughs)

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.750
Cause he got drunk.
- Oh right.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.490
- And they're trying to
wake him up. (laughs)

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:42.360
- [Nicolas] Yeah.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.950
- And they say, "Action",

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.478
and he just springs up. (laughs)

00:01:45.478 --> 00:01:46.311
- [Nicolas] That was great.

00:01:46.311 --> 00:01:47.310
That was funny.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.203
That was Tiffany.

00:01:48.203 --> 00:01:49.816
Tiffany did that.

00:01:49.816 --> 00:01:51.092
Action!
- Tiffany.

00:01:51.092 --> 00:01:52.172
Tiffany Haddish is it?

00:01:52.172 --> 00:01:53.190
- It's so fun.
- It's amazing.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.750
The cast is incredible,

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.060
but it's so amazing and narcissistic.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:57.990
- [Nicolas] Yes.
- Like the whole.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.030
It's just like action and go.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:00.880
And it's like,

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.050
it's so perfectly, like humorous perfect.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.580
- Thank you.
- It's really, really good.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.170
So you also play a young version

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.003
of yourself.
- Yeah.

00:02:08.003 --> 00:02:09.270
- Which is another great part.
- Yes.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.103
- Cause you,

00:02:10.103 --> 00:02:11.471
you make out with yourself.
- Yes.

00:02:11.471 --> 00:02:13.350
(all laughing)

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.748
Well that's wasn't

00:02:14.748 --> 00:02:15.793
in the script.
- It's the most narcissistic.

00:02:15.793 --> 00:02:17.580
It wasn't in the script?
- No, no.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.720
I put that in, because

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.925
that's what it felt like.
- I love you!

00:02:20.925 --> 00:02:21.958
I love you!

00:02:21.958 --> 00:02:23.547
(audience clapping)

00:02:23.547 --> 00:02:25.380
You put that in the script.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.213
There's this part.

00:02:26.213 --> 00:02:27.046
I don't wanna ruin the whole movie.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:27.879
There is so many great moments.

00:02:27.879 --> 00:02:29.430
- Let them.
- But it's like,

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.898
there's this moment
you're admiring yourself,

00:02:30.898 --> 00:02:32.760
and you're just like, yeah!

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.723
- It's like --
- Yeah.

00:02:33.723 --> 00:02:34.740
- It's amazing.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.530
- Well yeah, that
character's name is Nicki.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:40.140
He's the younger version
of so called Nick Cage.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.690
And I based that character.
- He's super narcissistic.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.380
- So arrogant. So
irreverent, so obnoxious.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:50.340
And I based him on my

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.530
when I was on the Wogan Show in England.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.570
I went on that show,

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.770
and I was promoting Wild at Heart.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.270
I did front hand springs,

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.710
and I was doing karate kicks,

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.180
and throwing money in the audience.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.260
The guy was awful.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.310
I was awful.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.480
I took my t-shirt off,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.620
put a leather jacket on.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.170
I go, "That's who I want to be

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.910
in the massive talent movie

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.539
to be picking on Nick Cage".

00:03:10.539 --> 00:03:12.120
- [Kelly] It was amazing.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.580
- But what happened was I said, okay.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.540
Well, this whole
experience for me is weird

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.610
